meta-microblx: bitbake layer for the microblx framework
=======================================================

This layer provides recipes for the [microblx](https://github.com/kmarkus/microblx)
real-time function block framework and its runtime dependencies
(LuaJIT modules, liblfds, ...).

Dependencies
------------

  URI: git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky
  branch: scarthgap (tested; layer compat reaches back to dunfell)

  URI: git://git.openembedded.org/meta-openembedded
  layers: meta-oe
  branch: scarthgap

Adding the layer to your build
------------------------------

Add the layer path to `BBLAYERS` in `bblayers.conf` as usual, or use
one of the kas configurations shipped in `kas/`:

```sh
$ kas build meta/meta-microblx/kas/ubx-bbb.yml         # BeagleBone Black
$ kas build meta/meta-microblx/kas/ubx-beagleplay.yml  # BeaglePlay
```

Recipes
-------

microblx comes in three flavors (all share `microblx.inc`):

- `microblx` -- latest release (0.9.2, `master`)
- `microblx-devel` -- pinned snapshot of the `dev` branch
- `microblx-latest` -- AUTOREV tip of the `dev` branch

```sh
$ bitbake microblx-latest
```

Further recipes:

- `microblx-build-tools` -- `ubx-tocarr` build helper
  (`BBCLASSEXTEND` native/nativesdk), needed when building external
  block projects
- `recipes-support/` -- runtime dependencies: `uutils`, `liblfds`
  (6.1.1), `luasocket-jit`, `lua-json`, `lua-compat53`,
  `lua-optparse`, `lua-lsdbus`/`luajit-lsdbus`, `ffi-reflect`,
  `cproto-native`
- `recipes-devtools/luaunit` -- Lua unit testing framework (used by
  the ptests)

PACKAGECONFIG options
---------------------

Set via e.g. `PACKAGECONFIG:pn-microblx-latest += "..."`:

| Option             | Default | Description                                                                                  |
|--------------------|---------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `USE_LFDS_611`     | on      | build the legacy `lfds_cyclic` iblock against liblfds 6.1.1 (deprecated, prefer `lfrb`)       |
| `BLOCK_WEBGRAPH`   | on      | webgraph visualization block (rdepends: `luasocket-jit`, `lua-json`)                          |
| `UBX_LOG_DAEMON`   | on      | build `ubx-log` with daemonization support (libdaemon, auto-detected by cmake)                |
| `BLOCK_LSDB_INTF`  | off     | D-Bus introspection/control block (rdepends: `luajit-lsdbus`, `lua-optparse`)                 |
| `USE_TIMESRC_TSC`  | off     | use the x86 TSC as timesource                                                                 |
| `USE_TIMESRC_CNTVCT` | off   | use the ARM generic counter (CNTVCT) as timesource                                            |
| `TRACING_SDT`      | off     | compile in USDT/SDT trace probes (build dep: `systemtap` for `sys/sdt.h`; no runtime deps)    |
| `TRACING_MARKER`   | off     | compile in ftrace `trace_marker` tracing                                                      |

`TRACING_SDT` and `TRACING_MARKER` are mutually exclusive; with
neither set, tracing is compiled out entirely (cmake `TRACING=OFF`).
See the "Tracing" section in the microblx README for usage.

Packaging notes
---------------

- `${PN}-ffi-headers` contains the small set of headers the LuaJIT
  FFI bindings parse at *runtime* (see `ubx_ffi_headers` in
  `lua/ubx.lua`); it is an install-time requirement of `${PN}`. All
  other headers go to `${PN}-dev` as usual.
- Examples are packaged in `${PN}-doc`, the Lua tests in `${PN}-test`.
- The Lua tests can be run on target as ptests: add `ptest` to
  `DISTRO_FEATURES`, install `ptest-runner` and `${PN}-ptest`, then
  run e.g. `ptest-runner microblx-latest`.

Patches
-------

Please submit patches via the github issue tracker
https://github.com/kmarkus/meta-microblx.
